Optional runtime animation library (not vendored)
-------------------------------------------------

Some video skills (talking-head-recut, music-to-video) may instruct users or
templates to load GSAP (GreenSock) from a CDN or a locally fetched copy.
GSAP is subject to GreenSock's own license (https://gsap.com/standard-license)
and is **not** redistributed as part of EvoFlow. Obtain and use it under terms
that apply to you.

CDPR / Cyberpunk fan-kit materials previously referenced by embedded-captions
are **not** included in this repository.

Liquid glass theme (MIT)
------------------------

`evopanel/vendor/liquid-glass-theme/` contains build-input sources adapted from
https://github.com/Rainpomelo/deepseek-harness-liquid-glass-theme (MIT).
See that folder’s LICENSE. Runtime UI uses EvoFlow’s `evopanel/src/lib/liquid-glass/`
modules generated/adapted from those sources — not the upstream DeepSeek/DSH package
identity.


Projects referenced for design / architecture inspiration
---------------------------------------------------------

EvoFlow is an independent product. During development we also studied (and in
places adapted ideas from) the following open-source agent projects. Linking
them here is attribution and thanks — it does **not** mean EvoFlow is a fork
of any of them, and it does **not** change this repository's primary license.

* Hermes Agent (Nous Research)
  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
  https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com
  (community nickname in Chinese: 爱马仕)
  Areas we looked at include gateway / IM channels, skills, memory plugins,
  and community-ops surface. Some memory-related paths under
  ``backend/packages/harness/evoflow/agents/memory_plugins/memory_port/``
  retain upstream-oriented naming; see file headers where present.

* OpenClaw
  https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw
  https://openclaw.ai
  (community nickname in Chinese: 小龙虾)
  Areas we looked at include multi-channel personal assistants, skills
  packaging, and gateway-style control-plane patterns.

* OpenAI Codex (CLI / agent tooling)
  https://github.com/openai/codex
  Areas we looked at include coding-agent UX, sandbox helpers, and local
  agent-loop patterns.

Other runtime / UI foundations are listed in the README acknowledgements
(LangGraph, LangChain, MCP, Tauri, etc.).

If an attribution is missing or a similarity needs a clearer notice, contact
cloud@evovexai.com or open a GitHub Issue; we will review and update this file.

Optional Runtime Dependencies (npm, not vendored)
-------------------------------------------------

EvoFlow may launch the following packages via ``npx`` when the user enables
Obsidian Knowledge Vault and clicks install/initialize. Source code of these
packages is **not** distributed as part of EvoFlow; licenses are determined by
their upstream repositories:

* obsidian-hybrid-search@0.13.22
  https://github.com/flowing-abyss/obsidian-hybrid-search
* obsidian-mcp-server@3.2.9
  https://github.com/cyanheads/obsidian-mcp-server

See docs/guides/integrations/obsidian-knowledge-vault.md.

